
# GN4 Guile Webservice Documentation

This is the documentation for setting gn-guile locally.

## 1. Channels Setup

Make sure your **channels file** includes the latest commits, especially `gn-machines`: 

```
;; guile_channels.scm
(list
 (channel
  (name 'gn-machines)
  (url "https://git.genenetwork.org/gn-machines")
  (branch "main")
  (commit "3b488840ff60a140f25dc1d2d24473b70a49fcc5"))

 (channel
  (name 'guix)
  (url "https://codeberg.org/guix/guix")
  (branch "master")
  (commit "0a4740705090acc4c8a10d4f53afc58c9f62e980"))

 (channel
  (name 'guix-forge)
  (url "https://git.systemreboot.net/guix-forge/")
  (branch "main")
  (introduction
   (make-channel-introduction
    "0432e37b20dd678a02efee21adf0b9525a670310"
    (openpgp-fingerprint
     "7F73 0343 F2F0 9F3C 77BF 79D3 2E25 EE8B 6180 2BB3"))))

 (channel
  (name 'guix-bioinformatics)
  (url "https://git.genenetwork.org/guix-bioinformatics")
  (branch "master")
  (commit "9b0955f14ec725990abb1f6af3b9f171e4943f77")))
  
```

>a Updating `gn-machines` to the latest commit fixes the previous `no code for module (config)` error. `-L ~/gn-machines` is no longer

## 2. Clone Repositories

### gn-guile
```

> git clone tux02.genenetwork.org:/home/git/public/gn-guile
or
>  https://git.genenetwork.org/gn-guile
```



### gn-docs
```

> git clone [https://git.genenetwork.org/gn-docs/](https://git.genenetwork.org/gn-docs/) ~/gn-guile-files/gn-docs

```

> Ensure `gn-docs-local-checkout` points to this path.

## 3. Running the Web Server

Navigate to `gn-guile` and start the server:

```

> guix shell --container --network --file=guix.scm 
> -- guile -L . --fresh-auto-compile -e main bin/gn-guile 8091

```

- `--container` runs in an isolated environment  
- `--network` allows container network access  
- Check API root:  
```

> curl [http://127.0.0.1:8091](http://127.0.0.1:8091)

```

Other endpoints:
```

> curl [http://127.0.0.1:8091/home/msk](http://127.0.0.1:8091/home/msk)
> curl [http://127.0.0.1:8091/home/aging](http://127.0.0.1:8091/home/aging)

```

### 3.1 Development with Emacs/Geiser
```

> guix shell --container --network --development --file=guix.scm 
> -- guile -L . --fresh-auto-compile --listen=1970 -e main bin/gn-guile 8091

```

- Connect via **Emacs-Geiser** on port `1970`  
- Update procedures live using `C-M-x`  
- Alternatives: [ares](https://git.sr.ht/~abcdw/guile-ares-rs) and [arei](https://git.sr.ht/~abcdw/emacs-arei)

## 4. Configuration Notes

`gn-docs-local-checkout` must exist:

```

> mkdir -p ~/gn-guile-files/gn-docs

```

Or pass it explicitly:

```

> guile -e main bin/gn-guile --gn-docs-local-checkout /home/kabui/gn-guile-files/gn-docs

```

- Inside `--container`, bind with:  
```

> --share=$HOME/gn-guile-files=/home/kabui/gn-guile-files

```
